os(x)| + 2|\sin(x)|$. The maximum value of $|\cos(x)| + |\sin(x)|$ is $\sqrt{2}$, which occurs when $|\cos(x)| = |\sin(x)| = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Therefore, the maximum value of $2|\cos(x)| + 2|\sin(x)|$ is $2\sqrt{2}$. Thus, the maximum value of $|1 + z| + |1 - z + z^2|$ is $2\sqrt{2}$. \boxed{2\sqrt{2}}
